{
  "id": "wavre",
  "title": "Wavre",
  "date": "18–19 June 1815",
  "blurb": "While Napoleon fights at Waterloo, Marshal Grouchy follows the Prussians down the Namur road and finds Thielmann's rearguard holding the Dyle at Wavre. The rain-swollen river runs in a deep valley; the town and its two stone bridges sit at the bottom, Bierges mill guards the crossing upstream, and Limal bridge lies far to the south. The Prussians hold the steep left-bank heights. Every bridge he fails to take is a Prussian corps that marches to Waterloo.",
  "hint": "The Dyle can only be crossed at the bridges: Wavre, Bierges mill and Limal. Storming the town head-on is costly; Limal turns the whole line, then climb to the Bierges heights and the Brussels road. Your guns on the right-bank heights see into the valley. Farms and the mill can be garrisoned.",
